# {{ project_name }}

A small C++17 StreamPU pipeline generated by Hulotte. The graph is explicit in `src/main.cpp`; edit the C++ directly.

## Build and run

Set `STREAMPU_ROOT` to the StreamPU source tree, then run:

```sh
# Configure the project using the StreamPU tree selected by STREAMPU_ROOT.
cmake -S . -B build
# Compile the pipeline and discovered custom modules.
cmake --build build
# Run the pipeline directly.
./build/{{ executable_name }}
# Run the same pipeline through CTest.
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

The initial pipeline connects `Source_random<int>` to the custom `PassThrough` module and a `Comparator` reference path. It executes three frames and exits with an error if any output element differs from the source.

Added custom modules live under `src/custom/`. Integrate their includes, instances, and socket bindings into `src/main.cpp` manually, replacing any existing binding to the same input socket. CMake discovers added `.cpp` files automatically. A file under `src/hw/` enables Verilator and must define a top-level module matching the filename.

Hardware wrappers use equal-length 32-bit integer frames and retain their RTL state across frames. A simulation timeout raises an error. To collect a VCD, pass a distinct output path as the adapter's second constructor argument. Trace paths are relative to the executable's working directory.
